   "hip": "one main roof mass with a ridge (or point) and slopes on all four sides",
   "complex": "two or more distinct roof masses or ridge directions of comparable size: L, T or U plans, cross gables, a wing or addition whose roof is at least about a fifth of the whole, or a large flat part beside a large pitched part",
